{
  "<div align=\"center\">\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/wordmark.svg#gh-light-mode-only\" width=\"220\" height=\"69\" alt=\"Papilot\"><img src=\"docs/assets/wordmark-dark.svg#gh-dark-mode-only\" width=\"220\" height=\"69\" alt=\"Papilot\"><br>**Next-Generation AI LaTeX Editor**\n\n# Don't read or write `.tex`<br>Just work on the <img src=\"docs/assets/pdf.svg\" width=\"34\" height=\"41\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"PDF\">\n\nA **new paradigm** for responsible writing and typesetting with AI.\n\n**[Download Papilot](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/releases/latest)** for <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/apple-dark.svg\"><img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/apple.svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture>&nbsp;macOS (Apple&nbsp;Silicon&nbsp;/&nbsp;Intel),<br><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/linux-dark.svg\"><img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/linux.svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture>&nbsp;Linux (AppImage / <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/ubuntu.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\">&nbsp;Ubuntu / <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/debian.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\">&nbsp;Debian / <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/nixos.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\">&nbsp;NixOS) or Windows (x64),<br>or run `npm install -g papilot`.\n\n<a href=\"https://papilot.ai\">\n<picture>\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero-compact-dark.png\">\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero-dark.png\">\n  <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero-compact.png\">\n  <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero.png\" alt=\"Papilot shows an AI edit as a typeset before-and-after on the PDF, with Accept, Reject and Comment.\" width=\"900\">\n</picture>\n</a>\n\n</div>\n\n## 📄 You care about the PDF<br>Not the `.tex` behind it\n\nPapers, theses, books, slides: readers only ever see the typeset page.<br>\n**So the page is where you should work, too.**\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm-compact-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm-compact.png\">\n    <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm.png\" alt=\"Writing LaTeX by hand, then checking LaTeX diffs from AI, and now Papilot: reviewing the PDF.\" width=\"900\">\n  </picture>\n</p>\n\n**No more compiling diffs in your head.**<br>\nA source diff makes you *imagine* the PDF. Papilot *shows* it to you, typeset.\n\n## 👉 Point at the page and say what you want\n\nMark a sentence, an equation or a figure, and write a note.<br>\n**Your agent finds the source. You never open a `.tex` file.**\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app-compact-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app-compact.png\">\n    <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app.png\" alt=\"Papilot with a box around an equation and a highlighted sentence on the PDF, each with a note, both added to the next task.\" width=\"900\">\n  </picture>\n</p>\n\n<a id=\"features\"></a>\n\n## 🔒 Your files stay yours\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/folder.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Plain files on your machine.** Every change lands in your Git history.\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/git.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Sync with coauthors through Git.** Pull, push, and let an agent resolve conflicts.\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/code.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Free and open source.** MIT licensed, for macOS, Linux and Windows.\n\n<a id=\"agents\"></a>\n\n## 🤖 Bring the AI agent you already use\n\n<!-- BEGIN AGENT ICONS -->\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"docs/guide.md#agents\">\n    <picture>\n      <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/compact-dark.svg\">\n      <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/desktop-dark.svg\">\n      <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/compact.svg\">\n      <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/desktop.svg\" alt=\"Codex, Claude, Cursor, Copilot, Grok, Antigravity, Kimi, GLM, DeepSeek, Qwen, OpenCode\" width=\"816\">\n    </picture>\n  </a>\n</p>\n<!-- END AGENT ICONS -->\n\n<a id=\"quick-start\"></a>\n\n## 🚀 Get started\n\n1. **Install.** [Download the app](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/releases/latest) for macOS, Linux or Windows, or run `npm install -g papilot` (Node.js 22.22+). You also need Git and TeX Live or MacTeX.\n2. **Open your project.** Choose the folder with your `.tex` files. Papilot builds the PDF.\n3. **Pick an agent.** Use the CLI login or API key you already have, then mark up the page.\n\nWant a sample first? Run `papilot demo`. Details are in the [guide](docs/guide.md#install-and-run).\n\n<a id=\"documentation-and-community\"></a>\n\n## 🤝 Community\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/issue.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Found a bug or missing a feature?** [Open an issue](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/issues/new/choose), even a rough one.\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/discussion.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Have a question or an idea?** [Start a discussion](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/discussions).\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/pull-request.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Become a contributor.** Pull requests are very welcome, including ones written with AI agents. Start with the [contributing guide](.github/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n\n---\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n<p data-language-switcher><sub><a href=\"README.md\">English</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.zh-CN.md\">简体中文</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.zh-Hant.md\">繁體中文</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.ja.md\">日本語</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.ko.md\">한국어</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.de.md\">Deutsch</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.fr.md\">Français</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.es.md\">Español</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.pt.md\">Português</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.it.md\">Italiano</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.sv.md\">Svenska</a></sub></p>\n\n</div>\n\n<p align=\"center\"><sub><a href=\"LICENSE\">MIT</a> © 2026 PapilotAI. Thanks to our friends at <a href=\"https://linux.do/\">LINUX DO</a>.</sub></p>\n": "<div align=\"center\">\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/wordmark.svg#gh-light-mode-only\" width=\"220\" height=\"69\" alt=\"Papilot\"><img src=\"docs/assets/wordmark-dark.svg#gh-dark-mode-only\" width=\"220\" height=\"69\" alt=\"Papilot\"><br>**Éditeur LaTeX IA de nouvelle génération**\n\n# Ne lisez ni n'écrivez de `.tex`<br>Travaillez directement sur le <img src=\"docs/assets/pdf.svg\" width=\"34\" height=\"41\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"PDF\">\n\nUn **nouveau paradigme** pour une rédaction et une composition responsables avec l'IA.\n\n**[Télécharger Papilot](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/releases/latest)** pour <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/apple-dark.svg\"><img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/apple.svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture>&nbsp;macOS (Apple&nbsp;Silicon&nbsp;/&nbsp;Intel)<br>et <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/linux-dark.svg\"><img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/linux.svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture>&nbsp;Linux (AppImage / <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/ubuntu.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\">&nbsp;Ubuntu / <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/debian.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\">&nbsp;Debian / <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/nixos.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\">&nbsp;NixOS) ou Windows (x64),<br>ou exécutez `npm install -g papilot`.\n\n<a href=\"https://papilot.ai\">\n<picture>\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero-compact-dark.png\">\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero-dark.png\">\n  <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero-compact.png\">\n  <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/hero.png\" alt=\"Papilot affiche une modification de l'IA sous forme de comparatif avant/après composé sur le PDF, avec les options Accepter, Rejeter et Commenter.\" width=\"900\">\n</picture>\n</a>\n\n</div>\n\n## 📄 Ce qui vous importe, c'est le PDF<br>Pas le `.tex` derrière\n\nArticles, thèses, livres, diapositives : les lecteurs ne voient jamais que la page composée.<br>\n**C'est donc aussi sur la page que vous devriez travailler.**\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm-compact-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm-compact.png\">\n    <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/paradigm.png\" alt=\"Écrire du LaTeX à la main, puis vérifier les diffs LaTeX de l'IA, et maintenant Papilot : la révision directement sur le PDF.\" width=\"900\">\n  </picture>\n</p>\n\n**Fini la compilation mentale des diffs.**<br>\nUn diff du code source vous oblige à *imaginer* le PDF. Papilot vous le *montre*, déjà composé.\n\n## 👉 Pointez la page et dites ce que vous voulez\n\nSélectionnez une phrase, une équation ou une figure, et rédigez une annotation.<br>\n**Votre agent trouve le code source. Vous n'ouvrez jamais de fichier `.tex`.**\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app-compact-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app-dark.png\">\n    <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app-compact.png\">\n    <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-showcase/notes-app.png\" alt=\"Papilot avec une équation encadrée et une phrase surlignée sur le PDF, chacune accompagnée d'une annotation, toutes deux ajoutées à la prochaine tâche.\" width=\"900\">\n  </picture>\n</p>\n\n<a id=\"features\"></a>\n\n## 🔒 Vos fichiers restent les vôtres\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/folder.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**De simples fichiers sur votre machine.** Chaque modification est enregistrée dans votre historique Git.\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/git.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Synchronisez avec vos coauteurs via Git.** Récupérez (pull), publiez (push) et laissez un agent résoudre les conflits.\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/code.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Gratuit et open source.** Sous licence MIT, pour macOS, Linux et Windows.\n\n<a id=\"agents\"></a>\n\n## 🤖 Utilisez l'agent IA que vous connaissez déjà\n\n<!-- BEGIN AGENT ICONS -->\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"docs/guide.md#agents\">\n    <picture>\n      <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark) and (max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/compact-dark.svg\">\n      <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/desktop-dark.svg\">\n      <source media=\"(max-width: 600px)\" srcset=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/compact.svg\">\n      <img src=\"docs/assets/readme-agents/desktop.svg\" alt=\"Codex, Claude, Cursor, Copilot, Grok, Antigravity, Kimi, GLM, DeepSeek, Qwen, OpenCode\" width=\"816\">\n    </picture>\n  </a>\n</p>\n<!-- END AGENT ICONS -->\n\n<a id=\"quick-start\"></a>\n\n## 🚀 Prise en main\n\n1. **Installation.** [Téléchargez l'application](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/releases/latest) pour macOS, Linux ou Windows, ou exécutez `npm install -g papilot` (Node.js 22.22+). Vous aurez également besoin de Git et de TeX Live ou MacTeX.\n2. **Ouvrez votre projet.** Choisissez le dossier contenant vos fichiers `.tex`. Papilot génère le PDF.\n3. **Choisissez un agent.** Utilisez la connexion CLI ou la clé API dont vous disposez déjà, puis annotez la page.\n\nVous voulez d'abord voir un exemple ? Exécutez `papilot demo`. Tous les détails figurent dans le [guide](docs/guide.md#install-and-run).\n\n<a id=\"documentation-and-community\"></a>\n\n## 🤝 Communauté\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/issue.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Vous avez trouvé un bug ou il vous manque une fonctionnalité ?** [Ouvrez un ticket](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/issues/new/choose), même succinct.\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/discussion.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Vous avez une question ou une idée ?** [Lancez une discussion](https://github.com/PapilotAI/papilot/discussions).\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/readme-icons/pull-request.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"> &nbsp;**Devenez contributeur.** Les pull requests sont les bienvenues, y compris celles rédigées avec des agents IA. Consultez le [guide de contribution](.github/CONTRIBUTING.md) pour commencer.\n\n---\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n<p data-language-switcher><sub><a href=\"README.md\">English</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.zh-CN.md\">简体中文</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.zh-Hant.md\">繁體中文</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.ja.md\">日本語</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.ko.md\">한국어</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.de.md\">Deutsch</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.fr.md\">Français</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.es.md\">Español</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.pt.md\">Português</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.it.md\">Italiano</a>&nbsp;· <a href=\"docs/readme/README.sv.md\">Svenska</a></sub></p>\n\n</div>\n\n<p align=\"center\"><sub><a href=\"LICENSE\">MIT</a> © 2026 PapilotAI. Merci à nos amis de <a href=\"https://linux.do/\">LINUX DO</a>.</sub></p>\n"
